1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:11,356
This is Petunia. Petunia is brave, Petunia is curious, and Petunia is the best paper-boat captain on Duke Street.

2
00:00:11,806 --> 00:00:15,986
Petunia: Captain Petunia, ready to sail! Dad, is the ocean ready?

3
00:00:16,436 --> 00:00:19,919
Dad: The ocean is one giant puddle, Captain. Ready when you are!

4
00:00:20,369 --> 00:00:23,202
Petunia: Three, two, one... launch!

5
00:00:23,652 --> 00:00:30,385
The little green boat bobbed across the puddle, past a sneaky leaf, around a pebble island.

6
00:00:30,835 --> 00:00:33,157
Dad: Whoa! She's going full speed!

7
00:00:33,607 --> 00:00:36,951
Petunia: That's because she's the fastest boat in the whole wide puddle!

8
00:00:37,401 --> 00:00:44,692
But somebody else was watching that boat. Somebody small, and fuzzy, and very, very sneaky.

9
00:00:45,142 --> 00:00:47,928
Petunia: Ow. Ow, ow, ow.

10
00:00:48,378 --> 00:00:50,979
Dad: Petunia? What's wrong, sweet pea?

11
00:00:51,429 --> 00:00:58,116
Petunia: My tummy. It's doing the twisty thing again. Like somebody's wringing out a wet towel inside me.

12
00:00:58,566 --> 00:01:03,721
Dad: Okay. Let's sit down on the step. Breathe with me, nice and slow.

13
00:01:04,171 --> 00:01:09,233
Endo-Monster: Hee hee hee! Squeeze, twist, grumble! Nobody can see me, and nobody will believe her!

14
00:01:09,683 --> 00:01:11,727
Petunia: The boat floated away without me.

15
00:01:12,177 --> 00:01:15,938
Dad: Then we'll make a new one. Captains always get another boat.

16
00:01:17,688 --> 00:01:27,626
The twisty days kept coming. Some days it was a little pinch. Some days it was so big that Petunia had to curl up in a ball.

17
00:01:28,076 --> 00:01:34,949
Petunia: Today is Maya's birthday party. There's a bouncy castle. And a piñata shaped like a unicorn.

18
00:01:35,399 --> 00:01:38,511
Petunia: And I'm here. In bed. With my tummy.

19
00:01:38,961 --> 00:01:47,459
Petunia was missing out. Missing parties. Missing recess. Missing the field trip to the aquarium.

20
00:01:47,909 --> 00:01:53,064
Petunia: Everybody thinks I'm just making it up. My teacher said every kid gets tummy aches.

21
00:01:57,314 --> 00:02:03,955
That night, Petunia couldn't sleep. She read her favorite book, but the words kept swimming around.

22
00:02:04,405 --> 00:02:11,603
Petunia: Maybe I ate too many grapes. Maybe I jumped in too many puddles. Maybe... maybe it's my fault.

23
00:02:12,053 --> 00:02:22,131
Endo-Monster: They have no idea it's me... Back to her tummy, and let's SEE where else I can hide... They will never FIND me!

24
00:02:22,581 --> 00:02:30,104
But that sneaky monster was wrong. It was not Petunia's fault. Not one little bit.

25
00:02:31,854 --> 00:02:36,962
Mom: Petunia, you've been so quiet. Is your tummy hurting again?

26
00:02:37,412 --> 00:02:43,403
Petunia: Mom, I think there's a monster in my tummy. And I think I made it come.

27
00:02:43,853 --> 00:02:51,376
Mom: Oh, baby. Come here. Look at me. Pain is never your fault. Never.

28
00:02:51,826 --> 00:02:55,124
Dad: And we believe you. Every single word.

29
00:02:55,574 --> 00:02:56,410
Petunia: You do?

30
00:02:56,860 --> 00:03:04,336
Mom: We do. You know your body better than anyone. When it tells you something is wrong, we listen.

31
00:03:04,786 --> 00:03:11,195
Dad: And while we listen, I brought reinforcements. One warm heating pad, and one rainbow fruit bowl.

32
00:03:11,645 --> 00:03:16,986
Petunia: Strawberries! And blueberries! And the banana slices are smiling!

33
00:03:17,436 --> 00:03:19,479
Dad: Every good captain needs a snack.

34
00:03:19,929 --> 00:03:23,598
Mom: And I brought you something too. Your yellow socks.

35
00:03:24,048 --> 00:03:25,255
Petunia: Why yellow?

36
00:03:25,705 --> 00:03:32,346
Mom: Yellow is a brave color. It's the color people wear to say, I see you, and you're not alone.

37
00:03:32,796 --> 00:03:37,905
Mom: Now let me teach you a trick for the twisty times. It's called dandelion breath.

38
00:03:38,355 --> 00:03:45,042
Mom: Pretend you're holding a dandelion. Breathe in through your nose, slowly, like you're smelling a flower.

39
00:03:45,492 --> 00:03:46,189
Petunia: Mmmmm.

40
00:03:46,639 --> 00:03:52,397
Mom: Now blow out softly through your mouth, and watch all the fluffy seeds float away.

41
00:03:52,847 --> 00:03:53,962
Petunia: Fwoooooo.

42
00:03:54,412 --> 00:04:01,981
Mom: Again. In, two, three. Out, two, three, four.

43
00:04:02,431 --> 00:04:05,357
Petunia: It's still there, but it's a little bit smaller.

44
00:04:05,807 --> 00:04:11,241
Mom: Dandelion breath doesn't make the monster leave. But it helps you stay the captain.

45
00:04:11,691 --> 00:04:16,613
Dad: And tomorrow, we're going to see a doctor who knows all about tummy monsters.

46
00:04:20,863 --> 00:04:26,343
Dr. Salem: Hello, Petunia. I'm Doctor Salem. I hear you've been having some very big tummy days.

47
00:04:26,793 --> 00:04:32,366
Petunia: Really big ones. They twist and pinch, and sometimes I can't go to school.

48
00:04:32,816 --> 00:04:36,392
Dr. Salem: Thank you for telling me. I hear you. And I believe you.

49
00:04:36,842 --> 00:04:39,303
Petunia: You believe me? Just like that?

50
00:04:39,753 --> 00:04:43,190
Dr. Salem: Just like that. Can you point to where it hurts the most?

51
00:04:43,640 --> 00:04:50,141
Petunia: Right here. Down low. And sometimes it goes all the way to my back.

52
00:04:50,591 --> 00:04:54,213
Dr. Salem: I want to show you something. This is one of my favorite picture books.

53
00:04:54,663 --> 00:05:02,790
Doctor Salem opened a big book. Inside was a drawing of a tummy, with bright little patches scattered around.

54
00:05:03,240 --> 00:05:10,578
Dr. Salem: Sometimes, little patches grow in places inside the body where they don't belong. Doctors call it endometriosis.

55
00:05:11,028 --> 00:05:14,836
Petunia: En-do-me-tri-o-sis. That's a really long word.

56
00:05:15,286 --> 00:05:23,042
Dr. Salem: It is! So lots of people just call it endo. Those patches can get sore and swollen, and that's what makes the twisty feeling.

57
00:05:23,492 --> 00:05:24,931
Petunia: So it's not my fault?

58
00:05:25,381 --> 00:05:31,790
Dr. Salem: Not even a little. You didn't eat the wrong thing or jump in the wrong puddle. It's just something some bodies have.

59
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:37,116
Petunia: So my monster has a name. Endo. The Endo-Monster.

60
00:05:37,566 --> 00:05:43,510
Dr. Salem: I like that name. And here's the good news. There are lots of ways we can help keep that monster quiet.

61
00:05:43,960 --> 00:05:50,833
Dr. Salem: To find out exactly where those patches are hiding, I'd like to take a look with a tiny camera, during a little surgery.

62
00:05:51,283 --> 00:05:54,023
Petunia: Surgery? Like... cutting?

63
00:05:54,473 --> 00:06:02,275
Dr. Salem: Just a few teeny tiny openings, smaller than your fingernail. You'll be fast asleep the whole time, and you won't feel a thing.

64
00:06:02,725 --> 00:06:05,140
Mom: And we'll be right there when you wake up.

65
00:06:05,590 --> 00:06:06,891
Petunia: Can I think about it?

66
00:06:07,341 --> 00:06:12,681
Dr. Salem: Of course. Brave doesn't mean not scared. Brave means asking all your questions.

67
00:06:16,931 --> 00:06:24,176
Surgery day came. Petunia wore a hospital gown with tiny stars on it, and her yellow socks.

68
00:06:24,626 --> 00:06:30,245
Nurse Mindy: Good morning, Captain! I'm Nurse Mindy. I heard you're the bravest sailor in the whole hospital.

69
00:06:30,695 --> 00:06:35,618
Petunia: I don't feel very brave. My heart is going boom, boom, boom.

70
00:06:36,068 --> 00:06:43,684
Nurse Mindy: That's okay. Lots of brave people have boom-boom hearts. Want me to tell you everything that's going to happen, step by step?

71
00:06:44,134 --> 00:06:46,316
Petunia: Yes, please. Every step.

72
00:06:46,766 --> 00:06:53,547
Nurse Mindy: First, I'll put a soft sticker on your hand. Then the sleepy medicine goes in, and it'll feel like a warm blanket.

73
00:06:53,997 --> 00:06:59,802
Nurse Mindy: While you sleep, Doctor Salem uses her tiny camera to find the endo patches and take them out.

74
00:07:00,252 --> 00:07:05,221
Nurse Mindy: And then you wake up in a cozy room, and your mom will be the first face you see.

75
00:07:05,671 --> 00:07:08,596
Petunia: Mom? Will you hold my hand?

76
00:07:09,046 --> 00:07:14,573
Mom: I'll hold your hand until you fall asleep, and I'll hold it again the second you wake up.

77
00:07:15,023 --> 00:07:20,224
Petunia: Okay. I'm scared. And I'm brave. Both at the same time.

78
00:07:20,674 --> 00:07:23,182
Mom: That's exactly what brave looks like.

79
00:07:23,632 --> 00:07:27,765
Nurse Mindy: Ready for the countdown, Captain? Let's count backwards from ten together.

80
00:07:28,215 --> 00:07:38,014
Petunia: Ten... nine... eight... I'm sailing my boat... seven... six...

81
00:07:38,464 --> 00:07:45,151
And before she reached five, Petunia was fast asleep, sailing on a warm and quiet sea.

82
00:07:46,901 --> 00:07:54,378
When Petunia opened her eyes, everything felt slow and fuzzy, like waking up from a long nap.

83
00:07:54,828 --> 00:07:56,593
Petunia: Mom? Is it over?

84
00:07:57,043 --> 00:08:02,151
Mom: It's over, baby. You did it. I've got your hand, just like I promised.

85
00:08:02,601 --> 00:08:06,084
Petunia: My tummy is sore. And my shoulders feel funny.

86
00:08:06,534 --> 00:08:13,500
Dad: The doctor said that's normal. The funny shoulders will go away in a day or two. Heating pad, coming right up.

87
00:08:13,950 --> 00:08:20,870
Dr. Salem: Hi, Captain. Everything went really well. We found the endo patches that were causing all that trouble, and we took them out.

88
00:08:21,320 --> 00:08:23,688
Petunia: So the Endo-Monster is gone forever?

89
00:08:24,138 --> 00:08:31,150
Dr. Salem: He's a lot smaller now. Sometimes endo can come back, so we'll keep checking on you. But you'll never have to face him alone.

90
00:08:31,600 --> 00:08:36,941
Petunia: I feel... relieved. Like I let out a really big dandelion breath.

91
00:08:38,691 --> 00:08:46,446
Petunia rested for many days. She watched cartoons, made paper boats, and ate a lot of smiling bananas.

92
00:08:46,896 --> 00:08:49,776
Endo-Monster: Hey! Where did all my hiding spots go?

93
00:08:50,226 --> 00:08:54,591
Petunia: I can see you now, Endo-Monster. And I'm not scared of you anymore.

94
00:08:55,041 --> 00:08:57,224
Endo-Monster: You... you can see me?

95
00:08:57,674 --> 00:09:06,172
Petunia: Yep. And next time you try a tummy twist, I'll have my dandelion breath, my heating pad, my doctor, and my family.

96
00:09:06,622 --> 00:09:09,780
Endo-Monster: Oh, rats. Not the grown-ups. Not the dandelions!

97
00:09:10,230 --> 00:09:14,549
Petunia: But what about all the other kids who have a monster, and nobody believes them?

98
00:09:16,299 --> 00:09:20,804
Petunia had an idea. A big, brave, yellow idea.

99
00:09:21,254 --> 00:09:27,245
Petunia: Everybody! Gather around! I'm starting a club. It's called the Endo Warriors!

100
00:09:27,695 --> 00:09:28,902
Friend: What's an Endo Warrior?

101
00:09:29,352 --> 00:09:37,804
Petunia: An Endo Warrior is anybody who has an Endo-Monster, or loves somebody who does. We wear yellow socks so we can find each other.

102
00:09:38,254 --> 00:09:43,177
Friend: I get really bad tummy days too. Sometimes I think I'm the only one.

103
00:09:43,627 --> 00:09:51,475
Petunia: You're not the only one. That's the first rule of the Endo Warriors. Nobody faces their monster alone.

104
00:09:51,925 --> 00:09:55,687
Petunia: Rule number two. We always believe each other.

105
00:09:56,137 --> 00:10:04,774
Petunia: Rule number three. When it hurts, tell a grown-up you trust. Right away. Even if you think they won't listen.

106
00:10:05,224 --> 00:10:13,862
Petunia: And rule number four. Dandelion breath! In through your nose... and out.

107
00:10:14,312 --> 00:10:15,288
Friend: Fwoooooo!

108
00:10:15,738 --> 00:10:18,803
Friend: Can I really join? I don't have yellow socks.

109
00:10:19,253 --> 00:10:23,571
Petunia: There's always room for you. Here, I brought an extra pair.

110
00:10:24,021 --> 00:10:30,709
Mom: Look at that. The bravest captain on Duke Street, with her very first crew.

111
00:10:31,159 --> 00:10:43,001
And that was how the Endo Warriors began. One brave girl, one pair of yellow socks, and a promise that nobody would ever face their monster alone.

112
00:10:43,451 --> 00:10:45,634
Petunia: Endo Warriors, set sail!

113
00:10:46,084 --> 00:10:48,406
The end... for now.

